{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pulls/180","id":4904172369,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABJE-7UQ","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pull/180","diff_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pull/180.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pull/180.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/180","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pulls/180/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pulls/180/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/180/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/statuses/ebc3b6bcd6e2c789c1c80c9e285193628567ea33","number":180,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"SET_CONFIGURATION: no notification when the configuration does not change; NO_SUCH_DESCRIPTOR for a missing index","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[A634]\n\nSET_CONFIGURATION: no notification without a change; NO_SUCH_DESCRIPTOR for a missing configuration.\n\nCloses #178\nCloses #179 (the acceptance item's \"testbench item A3\" was corrected on #179 to the SET_CONFIGURATION items W18d and W18d2; see \"Testbench item A3\" below)\n\n## What changes\n\nBoth fixes are in the SET_CONFIGURATION micro-program `E_SCFG` (`hdl/aecp/ucode/gen_ucode.py`). No RTL file changes, so there is no register-map, port or parameter change. No existing entry point moves, and the engine's µPC map is untouched.\n\n**#178: an unchanged index sends no unsolicited notification** (Milan v1.2 5.4.5.2: only a command that \"modifies the state\"; it narrows IEEE 1722.1-2021 7.4.7's \"on success this command also sends an unsolicited notification\").\n`E_SCFG` already compared the new index with the one in force and skipped `NOTIFY_ENQ` on equality, but with the operands in the wrong slots. The µCPU's `COMPARE` narrows only `ra` to the format and takes `rb` whole. The index in force was in `rb` (r6). Before the first SET, r6 is the image ENTITY's lane at byte 304, which holds `configurations_count` above `current_configuration`, so the two never compared equal. That is the silicon observation (SUCCESS, then u=1 to the registered controller). The fix is `COMPARE ra=6, rb=12`: r6 is narrowed to the index, and r12 holds the index alone. A real change still notifies once, to every registered controller except the requester.\n\n**#179: a configuration_index with no CONFIGURATION descriptor answers NO_SUCH_DESCRIPTOR** (IEEE 1722.1-2021 Table 7-141; 7.4.7.2 sets no status for it; owner decision 2026-10-17).\nThe range check (`index < configurations_count`) now branches to a new arm, `E_SCFGNSD` (ROM words 1553..1565, previously free). The arm answers NO_SUCH_DESCRIPTOR carrying the current index (7.4.7.1, \"the old value if it fails\"), through the same current-value overlay and response body as the other refusals. A command too short to carry the index stays BAD_ARGUMENTS.\n\n| Order | Case | Answer (cdl 16, current index) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | cdl < 16 | BAD_ARGUMENTS (unchanged) |\n| 2 | any Stream Input bound or Stream Output streaming | STREAM_IS_RUNNING, ahead of the lock and the index (Milan 5.4.2.5; unchanged) |\n| 3 | locked by another controller | ENTITY_LOCKED (unchanged) |\n| 4 | index >= configurations_count | **NO_SUCH_DESCRIPTOR** (was BAD_ARGUMENTS) |\n| 5 | otherwise | SUCCESS; one notification only if the index changed |\n\n## Records that follow the change\n\n- `hdl/aecp/ucode/aecp_commands.json`: SET_CONFIGURATION's status set gains NO_SUCH_DESCRIPTOR. F06.14 in `docs/architecture/06_aecp_engine.md` is regenerated by `scripts/check_aecp_commands.py --write`.\n- `tb/aecp_cmds/decode.json`: only the generated ROM digest changes, rewritten by `make -C tb/aecp_cmds record`. Every observed answer is unchanged.\n- `docs/00_MILAN_COMPLIANCE_REVIEW.md` §8 items 12 (#178) and 13 (#179) record both decisions with the issues' clauses. `docs/architecture/06_aecp_engine.md` §6.4 records the chain and the notes. `docs/architecture/09_verification.md` §8.1 names the new checks.\n\n## New checks, each with a planted mutant that fails it\n\n| Check | Mutant | Campaign |\n|---|---|---|\n| NP1a: SET_CONFIGURATION(0) to the image's configuration, store unset: SUCCESS byte-exact, nothing pushed to either controller | `configuration_compare_whole_lane` (the old COMPARE word), `configuration_unchanged_notifies` | `tb/pp_top/notify_mutants.py` |\n| NP1c: the same on the stored configuration | `configuration_unchanged_notifies` | notify |\n| NP1a/NP1c SUCCESS byte-exact | `configuration_success_reserved_dirty` | notify |\n| NP10: SET_CONFIGURATION(2) with sink 0 bound: STREAM_IS_RUNNING carrying 0, byte-exact | `configuration_running_route_dropped` | notify |\n| NP10b: that refusal pushes nothing | `configuration_refusal_notifies` | notify |\n| SC1/SC2 (section AX): SET_CONFIGURATION(2) and (0xFFFF), store unset, image index 1: NO_SUCH_DESCRIPTOR byte-exact carrying 1, cdl 16, no write, mark, notification or unsolicited frame | `scfg-range-bad-arguments`, `scfg-nsd-zero-body`, `scfg-nsd-stores`, `scfg-nsd-notifies`, `scfg-refusal-short-body` | `tb/pp_top/aecp_dispatch_mutants.py` |\n| SC3: GET_CONFIGURATION still reads 1 | `scfg-nsd-stores` | dispatch |\n\nW18d and W18d2 (the main run's SET_CONFIGURATION out-of-range checks) now expect NO_SUCH_DESCRIPTOR. The existing controls `enq_dropped_configuration` and `requester_not_excluded` still hold the change-side behaviour.\n\n## Testbench item A3\n\nIssue #179 says \"testbench item A3 asserts BAD_ARGUMENTS\" for SET_CONFIGURATION. In `tb/pp_top`, item A3 is READ_DESCRIPTOR with configuration_index 3. It is a READ_DESCRIPTOR check, and the assignment keeps READ_DESCRIPTOR unchanged. So A3 is left as it is. The suite's SET_CONFIGURATION out-of-range items are W18d and W18d2. Those are updated, and the new SC1-SC3 carry the planted mutants. Please confirm that this meets #179's A3 item before closing #179.\n\n## READ_DESCRIPTOR for a missing CONFIGURATION index (reported, not changed)\n\n- A CONFIGURATION descriptor_index the image lacks (configuration_index 0) is a locate miss: NO_SUCH_DESCRIPTOR with the 4-byte stub, cdl 20. That is the same status SET_CONFIGURATION now gives.\n- A configuration_index field at or past configurations_count is BAD_ARGUMENTS for every descriptor type, ENTITY and CONFIGURATION included (item A3). IEEE 1722.1-2021 7.4.5.1 says that field \"is ignored on receipt\" for ENTITY and CONFIGURATION reads. That is a separate question, left open here.\n\n## Validation\n\nAll results below were run locally, at base `22c139a4` and at head `ebc3b6bc`, with the CI-pinned simulator and conversion/synthesis versions. Nothing was piped.\n\n- `scripts/run_suites.sh`: rc 0 at both; 1,029,951 -> 1,029,973 checks. Every line is identical except the µPC gate (89 -> 90 entry points) and pp_top (10,470 -> 10,492: NP adds 6, SC adds 8 in each of the two builds that run AX). CI's executed requirement-tag half passes at both (226 evidence lines).\n- `scripts/lint_hdl.sh`, `scripts/gen_matrix.py --check`, the off-vendor portability elaboration and its guard grading: rc 0 at both, identical.\n- `make check`: rc 0 at both. Identical except 1,192 -> 1,195 links (the new review rows) and 578 -> 583 ID-scanned files (the new patches).\n- Every campaign that builds a changed file was run at both (dispatch, notify, aecp_cmds, aecp, ctr, gsi, name-write, maap, adp, name_state, acmp, d3), all rc 0. Every existing control fails the same checks at both. The only differences are expected: the ten new arms, one aecp_cmds generator arm whose failure text quotes its own planted ROM digest, and one aecp hazard diagnostic. In that diagnostic, three arms still fail HZ2, one clock later, because HZ1's SET_CONFIGURATION(0) on a fresh model is the no-change case and no longer enqueues a notification job.\n- The scratch parent at its dev commit, with the protocol-processor gitlink staged at base and then at head (never committed): the specification-facing BDD suite (406 scenarios), feature status, processor source lists, the source-style ratchets (unchanged budgets), whole-tree lint, the ROM ledger and the processor's out-of-context pricing all pass at both, with identical results apart from the new ROM digest and the Python line count. The pricing is unchanged area to the cell. Two parent gates fail identically at base and head, for reasons this change does not touch: the submodule pin record (any moved gitlink), and three test-evidence dispositions for campaign files already on processor main. The latter pass once the parent adds those dispositions.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-17T21:42:30Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T21:44:20Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"cd0719da2436fe20dae574b5dc5a36c3a8cbf6a9","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Mister-M-alt:178-179-set-configuration","ref":"178-179-set-configuration","repo":{"id":1330554057,"node_id":"R_kgDOT06kyQ","name":"protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan","full_name":"Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan","owner":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":null,"homepage":null,"language":"C++","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"watchers":0,"open_issues_count":5,"open_issues":5,"size":20125,"default_branch":"main","has_